1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:01,149
Lesson four.

2
00:00:01,149 --> 00:00:05,498
AI tools are useful, but they are also online services.

3
00:00:05,498 --> 00:00:13,800
In this lesson you will learn what never to share, and how to keep your accounts safe while you use them.

4
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:18,889
A good rule is to treat every AI chat like a public place.

5
00:00:18,889 --> 00:00:23,983
Depending on the tool, your messages may be stored or reviewed.

6
00:00:23,983 --> 00:00:29,400
So never type anything that would hurt you if someone else read it.

7
00:00:29,800 --> 00:00:39,504
Never share passwords or one time codes, wallet recovery phrases and private keys, or ID numbers, bank cards and your home address.

8
00:00:39,504 --> 00:00:43,800
No honest service needs these things in a chat with an AI.

9
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:46,968
Be careful with other people's data too.

10
00:00:46,968 --> 00:00:49,043
Do not paste private messages.

11
00:00:49,043 --> 00:00:57,000
Remove names and details before you ask for help, and ask permission before you upload someone's photo or document.

12
00:00:57,400 --> 00:00:58,816
Build safer habits.

13
00:00:58,816 --> 00:01:12,600
Use strong and different passwords, turn on two step login, and look at the privacy settings of each tool, such as chat history and whether your data can be used to improve the service.

14
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:15,558
Beware of fake AI websites and apps.

15
00:01:15,558 --> 00:01:18,046
Copy cat apps can steal your login.

16
00:01:18,046 --> 00:01:27,000
Install apps only from official stores, and type the official address yourself instead of clicking links from messages or ads.

17
00:01:27,400 --> 00:01:30,484
At work or at school, follow the rules.

18
00:01:30,484 --> 00:01:38,391
Do not upload confidential documents or customer data to a public AI tool unless you are allowed to.

19
00:01:38,391 --> 00:01:41,000
When you are not sure, ask first.

20
00:01:41,400 --> 00:01:46,373
A simple rule to remember: if anything asks you for a secret, stop.

21
00:01:46,373 --> 00:01:52,089
Next lesson: how to use AI to learn faster, without losing your own thinking.

22
